// Cap token exchange at 30 per hour per user.
//
// Counts `ExchangeToken` responses in this user's recent history — the
// workload-identity and agent credential path, which is automated and can
// run far faster than a human login. The threshold is higher than the
// issuance cap because a single workload legitimately re-exchanges on
// every credential expiry.
//
// Enforcement is best-effort: audit writes on this path are
// fire-and-forget, so a dropped write undercounts by one.
@id("exchange_rate_limit")
forbid (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"ExchangeToken", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (count_within(1h, Vouch::Action::"ExchangeToken"::response{ callerPrincipal: principal })) == n
        && n >= 30
    )
};
